Revo OS 
=> running on [kernel.zig](https://github.com/xt9y/kernel.zig) => a standalone MIT-derived x86-64 Zig kernel
=> Zig 0.17.0, QEMU and xorriso are required

    brew install zig qemu xorriso 
    make init compile run

Creates ./.build/disk.img (16 MiB)
The file persists across make clean, make distclean deletes it

Kernel resources are configured in kernel.config.zig, without editing ./kernel/.
Defaults come from kernel/src/config_defaults.zig.
Override once with: make run ZIG_OPTIONS='-Dmax-tasks=16 -Dprocess-code-pages=8 -Dheap-mib=64'
Settings take effect at build time and are validated for memory-layout conflicts.

The only language-dependent file is bridge/app.zig 
Hardware and scheduling are implemented by the independent ./kernel/ git submodule

| serial_puts(text) => Write to COM1 
| time_ms() => Milliseconds since PIT timer started (configured pit-hz resolution) 
| disk_sectors() => Detected IDE sector count, zero if absent 
| disk_read_hex(lba) => Read 512 bytes as 1024 ASCII hex characters 
| disk_write_hex(lba, hex) => Write one 512-byte sector from exactly 1024 hex digits 
| fb_width(), fb_height() => Framebuffer size, zero when unavailable 
| fb_pixel(x,y,rgb), fb_clear(rgb) => Pixel/clear operations on 32-bit RGB framebuffer 
| proc_spawn_hex(code) => Spawn raw position-independent x86-64 bytes in ring 3, up to process-code-pages * 4096 
| proc_count(), proc_state(pid) => Process status 
